{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b9c5b192c17a37ff","name":"Veltiss-2 Airspeeder","source":{"id":"source:reference-b9c5b192c17a37ff","title":"Veltiss-2 Airspeeder","revision":20339,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:39:49Z","sha256":"b5d86c5b6dbcf3d5d5e5d9849ddf1d22dd69319d209bf0ad66b17564688cef94","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20339","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Veltiss-2%20Airspeeder&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b9c5b192c17a37ff","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Another Airspeeder from a company that managed to profit from the turmoil surrounding the Yuuzhan Vong Invasion, the Veltiss-2 Airspeeder is a fast and lightweight vessel well suited to use on worlds where the urban sprawl puts large distances between common travel destinations. On worlds such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", where an Imperial delegate might be required to travel from one side of a continent to the other in the course of their day-to-day duties, the Veltiss-2 makes such a trip manageable. With the Veltiss-2, the Desler Gizh Outward Mobility Corporation made the transition from an Outer Rim upstart to a company catering to the wealthy elite on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," and other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Worlds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Worlds?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Veltiss-2 is a newer model Airspeeder that can be both open-topped or closed-cabin, depending on the needs of the pilot. When in open-top mode, the Veltiss-2 uses microrepulsor technology to create a \"virtual hard top\" that generates a nearly frictionless field, allowing the Airspeeder to maintain a slim, aerodynamic profile while protecting the pilot and passengers from the high winds associated with traveling at three-quarters the speed of sound. This repulsor field doesn't protect the passenger entirely, allowing them to enjoy good weather, though typically the owner of a Veltiss-2 will use the closed-cabin configuration during inclement weather. The Veltiss-2 Airspeeder also boasts significant advancements in pilot assistance technology, including traffic-pattern analytics software that makes it easier to navigate urban traffic lanes at such high speeds.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Moff ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyna Calixte"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyna_Calixte","referenceId":"reference:1aa3c5b4469bd375"}," owns a Veltiss-2 Airspeeder, which she uses to move about ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Veltiss-2 Airspeeder Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":